 "text": "Hey, good to have you here. How are you? Rough drawings look stiff because you think in smooth lines. Try using tiny lines, and draw over them if they don' turn out. Then draw with simple shapes instead of lines. A simple sketch can give the teacher enough information. Spend a few minutes each day on simple drawing exercise, like the one at the back of this book. Or draw your breakfast while it' still on plate. Don't worry. Rough drawings are way more friendly than photocopies. The key is doing several quick drawings, not one that looks good.",
